			"notes": "# CraftUI Stable Release\n\nNGL, creating a \"stable\" release is a little bit nerve-wracking, but I feel like the CraftUI API is at a point where I can finally consider it \"production-ready\".\n\nFrom here on out, CraftUI will maintain backwards-compatibility in line with Semantic Versioning. However,  Minecraft's API changes quite frequently. I'll strive to maintain backwards-compatibility across versions, and when that's not possible, a new major version will release.\n\nTo use this release, add this to your build script:\n\n```groovy\nrepositories {\n    // ...\n    maven { url = 'https://jitpack.io' }\n}\n```\n```\ndependencies {\n    // ...\n    modImplementation 'com.github.Igrium:CraftUI:1.0.0\"\n}\n```"
		}
